Data Structures and Algorithms – Midterm Examination

Question 1 (5 Marks):
What is the time complexity of Binary Search? Explain briefly.

Answer:
Binary Search has a time complexity of O(log n).

It follows the divide-and-conquer strategy. In each iteration, the algorithm
checks the middle element of the sorted array against the target value.

If the target is less than the middle element, the search proceeds in the
left half of the array. If the target is greater, the search proceeds in the
right half.

Thus, with every step, half of the remaining elements are discarded. Because
the search interval keeps shrinking by a factor of two, the number of required
comparisons increases logarithmically with the number of elements.

Therefore, the overall time complexity of Binary Search is O(log n).